=== layout: subsection

# Quiz

=== layout: two-panels

# *Quiz System Information*

@left

- 20 points; 20-34 questions
- MC\: 1 point; matching\: 1/2 per choice
- 20-30 minutes; about 1-1.5 min/question
- Normally: backtracking allowed; random order
- Limited calculations
- Both attempts\: (individual + group)/2
- Example\: (14 + 20)/2 = 17

@right

- Individual\: current course assessment platform
- Opens 20 hours before class
- Due BEFORE class
- Optional group\: during class
- 3-4 students; form a group in class
- Group score: at least 18/20; curve if needed

=== layout: one-panel

# *Optional Group Quizzes*

@body

- Complete the individual attempt before class.
- If you complete both attempts, your quiz score is their average.
  - Example: (14 + 20)/2 = 17.
- If you skip the optional group attempt, your individual score is your final quiz score.
- Tell me before the quiz/exam if you need to discuss an absence.

@citation

https://vosslab.github.io/syllabus/fall_2026/genetics/ASSIGNMENTS_AND_GRADING/

=== layout: one-panel

# *Low Quiz Grades*

@body

- How can I do better in this class?
- Did you complete the relevant assignments before taking the quiz?
  - The assignments and quizzes mostly have the same questions.
- Did you retake the relevant assignments and make sure you understood the questions? Did you retake them until you had a grade you were happy with?
  - The assignments and quizzes mostly have the same questions.

